====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  If the cos column is high, both savings hold in ONE circuit: G-independence
  from the phase readout and log-M width from the design register. The QPE
  ladder only ever touches `sys` under control of `anc`, so it cannot see
  what the param register encodes - the structural argument, now built.

  IF IT IS LOW, the phase readout does not survive the design encoding and
  the reason is the finding. Note v106 found exactly that for twirl_cal, but
  for a reason that does NOT apply here: there the register acts by
  CONJUGATION, so H_sigma is isospectral and a phase carries no signal. Here
  the register changes the STATE, so energies genuinely move.

  WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW. The QPE ladder's depth is the (2^k-1)*tau0
  evolution ladder that killed V5 on hardware (survival 0.098 at Heisenberg
  N=6). Qubit width and circuit count are what this file measures; DEPTH is
  the cost that moved, and it is unchanged by the design register.

  SCOPE. Heisenberg N=4,6, efficient_su2 reps=1, 4 ancillas, 32768 shots,
  3 seeds, R=0.45, no noise model, no hardware.
